::ingredients

(cocoa-nut, grated) 1/4lb
(white sugar, powdered) 1/4lb
(butter, fresh) 3 1/2oz
(egg white) 6
(wine and brandy, mixed) 1 table-spoonful
(rose-water) 1/2 tea-spoonful
(puff-paste) enough to cover bottom and sides and edges of soup-plate
(granulated sugar) as needed for top
(water, cold) as needed for washing

::equipment

(knife)
(towel, clean)
(soup-plate)
(oven)

::instructions

(cocoa-nut) <break> <peel, thin brown skin with knife> <wash, cold water> <dry, clean towel>
    <weigh, 1/4lb> <grate, very fine, into soup-plate>
{butter mixture} = (butter) + (white sugar) <cream>
    + (wine and brandy) + (rose-water) <add, gradually>
(egg white) <beat, until they stand alone on the rods>
    <stir, gradually into butter mixture>
(cocoa-nut) <sprinkle, gradually into mixture, stir hard>
{mixture} <stir, very well>
(puff-paste) <line, bottom and sides and edges of soup-plate>
    + {mixture} <fill> <bake, moderate oven, ~30m>
    <cool>
    + (granulated sugar) <sprinkle>

::source
<<<
---
title: "Cocoa-nut Pudding"
tags: ['cocoa', 'dessert', 'pudding']
date: 1832-01-01
author: "Miss Leslie"
---

## Ingredients

- A quarter of a pound of cocoa-nut, grated.
- A quarter of a pound of powdered white sugar.
- Three ounces and a half of fresh butter.
- The whites only of six eggs.
- A table-spoonful of wine and brandy mixed.
- Half a tea-spoonful of rose-water.

## Directions

1. Break up a cocoa-nut, and take the thin brown skin carefully off, with a knife. Wash all the pieces in cold water, and then wipe them dry, with a clean towel. Weigh a quarter of a pound of cocoa-nut, and grate it very fine, into a soup-plate.
2. Stir the butter and sugar to a cream, and add the liquor and rose-water gradually to them.
3. Beat the whites only, of six eggs, till they stand alone on the rods; and then stir the beaten white of egg, gradually, into the butter and sugar. Afterwards, sprinkle in, by degrees, the grated cocoa-nut, stirring hard all the time. Then stir all very well at the last.
4. Have ready a puff-paste, sufficient to cover the bottom, sides, and edges of a soup-plate. Put in the mixture, and bake it in a moderate oven, about half an hour.
5. Sprinkle granulated sugar over it, when cool.
>>>
